WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:05.232
Hey Youtubers it's Charlie.This is going to be my Game of Thrones Episode 4 video.

00:00:05.232 --> 00:00:06.609
Lots of exciting stuff to talk about.

00:00:06.609 --> 00:00:11.609
I feel like the show did everything short of screaming in confirming one of the biggest fan theories from the books.

00:00:11.609 --> 00:00:13.520
So we'll talk about that that stuff.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:15.320
And new round of the giveaway starts now.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.560
All you have to do to enter is be a subscriber and leave a comment on this video

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.240
Just careful for spoilers as we get started.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:24.339
So this is gonna be Top 7 moments just because there was a whole lot of extra stuff in this episode.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:28.140
Starting with #7 - Jorah is taking Tyrion to Daenerys. 

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:31.280
This is right out of the books, so it wasn't a huge surprise.

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:34.916
The tease was in the previous episode so that he was taking him to the Queen.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:39.200
Tyrion initially thought that it was his sister, but then he remembers who Jorah is 

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:44.400
and that he had been informing Varys in the small council on Daenerys in the earlier seasons.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.057
"Remind me how you were serving her inside a brothel"

00:00:47.557 --> 00:00:54.523
Well when you think about it, if he'd been working for Varys the whole time and Varys had secretly been part of the Targaryen Restoration

00:00:54.740 --> 00:01:01.740
Maybe in spying on Daenerys, he was inadvertently helping her or at least helping Varys make decisions based on where she was at.

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:02.926
That's just a theory.

00:01:02.926 --> 00:01:06.366
If you take it in the literal context - yes, he was a traitor to her.

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:09.226
Initially, it's just that Robert was the one that was calling all the shots.

00:01:09.226 --> 00:01:12.356
He's like, "I wanna spy on Daenerys right now. I want to murder her."

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:15.832
Varys, as Master of Whisperers, was responsible for hiring Jorah.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:18.040
I know everyone is wondering where Varys is now.

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:19.900
We'll probably find out next week. He'll probably be back.

00:01:20.055 --> 00:01:25.575
Onto #6 - Cersei reinstates the Faith Militant and they arrest Loras for being gay.

00:01:25.691 --> 00:01:32.691
My favorite quote from the Cersei scenes this week: "There's a sinner in our very midst, shielded by gold and privilege."

00:01:32.691 --> 00:01:34.309
She's was talking about Loras.

00:01:34.309 --> 00:01:40.759
The double meaning and the kind of look in the High Sparrow's eyes are that Cersei is a sinner shielded by gold and privilege.

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:42.910
"May they all be judged justly"

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:45.282
Right now though, it's only gone as far as Loras.

00:01:45.302 --> 00:01:49.623
And as we can see from Margaery being so pissed, Tommen isn't able to do shit about it.

00:01:49.623 --> 00:01:52.540
They just want to put Tommen forward as an ineffectual leader.

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:55.149
He's a little boy so you can't be too mad at him.

00:01:55.149 --> 00:01:58.149
The show aged him up quite a bit. He almost looks like a teenager.

00:01:58.149 --> 00:02:02.134
In the books, he is way younger. He's still a toddler. He's like a pudgy little kid.

00:02:02.134 --> 00:02:07.733
The downside is that last week when they had sex, that's probably going to be the last that you see that for a long time.

00:02:07.733 --> 00:02:10.949
There's no way that Margaery is gonna give it up while Loras is still in chains.

00:02:10.949 --> 00:02:14.136
For those that are wondering, he's actually being held at Baelor's Sept.

00:02:14.136 --> 00:02:19.088
So, expect to see a trial-type situation, you know, and a twist of what happened to Tyrion last year.

00:02:19.088 --> 00:02:22.532
He was put on trial and got steam rolled by the justice system.

00:02:22.532 --> 00:02:24.956
Now, thanks to Cersei, there's a new law man in town.

00:02:24.956 --> 00:02:27.941
And he's going to steam roll anyone he thinks is committing sin.

00:02:27.941 --> 00:02:29.970
I'm kind of digging bad-ass Lancel too.

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:32.449
He is way better now than he was in Season 1.

00:02:32.449 --> 00:02:36.723
That's the seven pointed star. That's the symbol of the church that they're carving into their foreheads.

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:41.403
Eventually, they're probably going to find out that Tommen is also the son of twinsest.

00:02:41.403 --> 00:02:44.898
If you could hear in that background shot in the crowd shot when he went to the sept,

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:49.846
they were screaming "Bastard!" at him - he seemed a little confused like he didn't totally understand what was going on.

00:02:49.846 --> 00:02:52.845
But that's going to come back. That's just like a hint of things to come.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:55.780
Onto #5 - Jaime and Bronn arrive at Dorne

00:02:55.940 --> 00:03:01.400
So just a reminder - what they're doing is they're trying to infiltrate the Water Gardens to get Myrcella out.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:03.647
They just want to get her and come back to King's Landing.

00:03:03.647 --> 00:03:08.719
Jaimie,unlike the Sand Snakes, doesn't want to start a war - like an all out war with Dorne.

00:03:08.719 --> 00:03:09.830
That's why it's only the two of them.

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:12.460
Jaimie and Bronn are like the new Jaimie and Brienne.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:13.800
Just absolute comedic relief.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.140
Along with some really good action scenes.

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:19.180
They even gave a shout-out to Tarth as they were passing by.

00:03:19.183 --> 00:03:22.120
Turns out it is not full of sapphires, as Jaimie said.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:28.500
There is just a bunch of really good one-liner moments, but I love that Jaimie is now using his hand as a defensive device.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:30.227
Although it was totally on accident.

00:03:30.227 --> 00:03:33.207
And he wants to die in the arms of the woman he loves.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:37.980
Yes, I do think he is talking about Brienne, even if he is not willing to admit it out loud.

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:43.160
I do think there's still a part of him that loves Cersei, just not in the way that he loved her in the past.

00:03:43.185 --> 00:03:48.708
I think he feels more of an obligation to Cersei because she's family - because she's the mother of his children.

00:03:48.708 --> 00:03:53.853
And he's gone into like full on dad-mode. "It has to be me. I have to be the one that rescues her."

00:03:53.853 --> 00:03:58.078
So in addition to waiting for like an all-out Jaimie and Brienne love scene,

00:03:58.429 --> 00:04:04.589
now we need to wait for a scene when Jaimie openly tells one of his children "I am your father."

00:04:04.589 --> 00:04:06.498
Onto #4 - Meet the Sand Snakes

00:04:06.498 --> 00:04:09.164
This is T-ing up the Arianne Martell plot from the books.

00:04:09.164 --> 00:04:11.554
Starting a war with King's Landing.

00:04:11.554 --> 00:04:14.163
Whether or not they're successful remains to be seen

00:04:14.163 --> 00:04:17.721
because Doran Martell, as they said, wants to keep the peace.

00:04:17.721 --> 00:04:24.059
He has his own plans though. You know, just because they say he wants peace doesn't mean that he isn't going to do anything about Oberyn's death.

00:04:24.059 --> 00:04:29.042
For now though, we just have to wait for a potential meeting between Jaimie and Bronn and the Sand Snakes.

00:04:29.042 --> 00:04:32.340
I'll add a link in the description for the Sand Snakes video I just did.

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:35.453
It just explains some of the differences between the show and the books.

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:41.880
This episode was really just the first introduction to them - so it's gonna be a few more episodes before we see what their characters are like on the show.

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:46.420
Onto #3 - Melisandre tries to make a shadow baby with Jon Snow

00:04:46.424 --> 00:04:50.193
"There is great power in you. You resist it, that's your mistake.

00:04:50.193 --> 00:04:52.933
Power to make light. Power to create shadows."

00:04:52.933 --> 00:04:56.845
Don't you just wonder how powerful a Jon Snow's shadow baby would be.

00:04:56.845 --> 00:04:59.032
There really is no benchmark for stuff like that.

00:04:59.032 --> 00:05:04.332
You have to assume that the more powerful the blood, the more powerful whatever Melisandre conjurs up ends up being.

00:05:04.332 --> 00:05:08.812
I guess it depends on how powerful you think Jon Snow's blood is versus Stannis.

00:05:08.812 --> 00:05:11.795
That's an argument that'll have to wait until after like the final season.

00:05:11.795 --> 00:05:16.155
For right now, the show is positioning both Stannis and Jon Snow as heroes.

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:18.960
That was what that whole Shireen scene with Stannis was about -

00:05:18.982 --> 00:05:22.297
showing that he's a very caring person in his own cold way.

00:05:22.297 --> 00:05:26.887
But all this Melisandre making sex eyes at Jon Snow is starting to make a little more sense

00:05:26.887 --> 00:05:30.649
given the context of some of the other scenes that have to do with his parentage.

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:35.920
Onto #2 - The show officially starts pushing R + L= J

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:38.954
Some of you probably expected this to come at a certain point.

00:05:38.954 --> 00:05:40.180
Some of you might have pooped your pants.

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:41.798
Some probably still don't believe it.

00:05:41.798 --> 00:05:47.613
Just taking the show at it's word, assuming Littlefinger was not lying and Ser Barriston Selmy is not lying

00:05:47.613 --> 00:05:53.013
and I definitely don't think he was lying - they're trying to position Rhaegar Targaryen as a nice person

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:55.492
who was in love with Lyanna Stark.

00:05:55.492 --> 00:05:59.328
"How many tens of thousands had to die because he chose your aunt."

00:05:59.328 --> 00:06:04.491
The crown of roses blue as frost also ties in with the really big prophecy with the show.

00:06:04.521 --> 00:06:08.961
Rhaegar Targaryen was obsessive about the prophecy - the prince who was promised.

00:06:08.961 --> 00:06:11.932
That's why everyone thinks that that is Jon Snow.

00:06:11.932 --> 00:06:14.232
He's like the secret prince that was promised.

00:06:14.232 --> 00:06:18.245
It's just that the prophecy describes a blue rose growing in a wall of ice.

00:06:18.245 --> 00:06:21.962
So you have Jon Snow, the blue rose, that was born of Lyanna Stark

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:25.420
up at a wall of ice, you know as in "The Wall" literally.

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:28.847
Dan and Dave aren't really big on doing prophecies on the TV show.

00:06:28.847 --> 00:06:35.235
They did kind of do Maggie the Frog, which is a prophecy, but I don't think they're going to get too crazy with that stuff in the future.

00:06:35.264 --> 00:06:41.804
Hopefully we'll just start to see more clues, like more characters, start to point evidence at the R+L= J theory.

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:46.460
As for right now, the best evidence is what Ser Barriston Selmy said and what Littlefinger said.

00:06:46.503 --> 00:06:49.422
But the tourney at Harrenhal is a really famous event.

00:06:49.422 --> 00:06:52.007
Rhaegar Targaryen, really great jouster, won the tournament

00:06:52.007 --> 00:06:57.274
 crowned Lyanna Stark instead of his wife, Elia Martell, Doran and Oberyn's sister

00:06:57.274 --> 00:06:58.556
causing everyone to lose their shit

00:06:58.556 --> 00:07:02.544
including Robert Bartheon, who Lyanna Stark was promised to.

00:07:02.544 --> 00:07:08.598
And just to reiterate, Robert's Rebellion didn't start because Rhaegar Targaryen obsconded with Lyanna Stark.

00:07:08.598 --> 00:07:12.626
It started because the Mad King was executing a bunch of nobles and their sons.

00:07:12.875 --> 00:07:18.075
But onto my #1 WTF moment - Grey Worm and Barriston Selmy look like they're dead

00:07:18.075 --> 00:07:24.119
The Sons of the Harpy lay a trap for the Unsullied and Grey Worm and Barriston Selmy kind of get caught up in it.

00:07:24.119 --> 00:07:31.033
Ever since that moment when Barriston Selmy left King's Landing and said "I could cut through all of you like a carving knife through a cake,"

00:07:31.033 --> 00:07:32.681
they had to show off some of his skills.

00:07:32.681 --> 00:07:37.794
He's a really old person, so if he's this good now, imagine how good he was in his prime.

00:07:37.794 --> 00:07:42.074
I also saw a lot of you guys complaining on Twitter that Grey Worm seemed like he went down too easy.

00:07:42.074 --> 00:07:45.482
They just - they want you to wonder whether or not they're going to survive.

00:07:45.482 --> 00:07:52.465
There is a promo for next week's episode. Just because it's kind of spoilery, it kind of answers some of those questions, I won't talk about it here.

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:54.840
But if you guys have seen it, just use spoiler tags.

00:07:54.965 --> 00:07:57.994
Here's my big question for you guys: What was your favorite moment from the episode?

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:03.720
And do you feel like, based on the evidence presented in this episode, R +L= J?

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:07.980
During the scene where Barriston was explaining Rhaegar's singing to Daenerys,

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:11.120
they also casually dismissed the threat of Hizdahr.

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:15.840
So, I feel like that's also a kind of warning bell that he is associated with the Sons of the Harpy.

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:18.150
Whether or not he's actually leading them remains to be seen.

00:08:18.150 --> 00:08:21.694
Unless they roll out some other big bad, I feel like he is the one calling the shots.

00:08:21.694 --> 00:08:24.092
So much great stuff in this episode.

00:08:24.092 --> 00:08:28.119
Sansa also gets to have some really interesting times while Littlefinger is gone.

00:08:28.119 --> 00:08:30.435
"I'll be a married woman by the time you get back."

00:08:30.460 --> 00:08:37.160
The big question with her storyline is: What is she going to do to try and out maneuver Roose Bolton and Ramsay Bolton?

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:40.220
If you're a little confused about Littlefinger's grand scheme here,

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:45.580
in the last episode, he was talking to Roose Bolton about forming an alliance against King's Landing.

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:50.380
But now, in the crypts, he was talking to Sansa about forming an alliance with Stannis

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:52.780
who is going to try to get rid of Roose Bolton.

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:57.720
Add to that, that Cersei is calling him to King's Landing. So Cersei still thinks of him as an ally.

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:04.664
So right now, Littlefinger has like a giant list of opponents that he is all trying to form alliances with at the same time.

00:09:04.664 --> 00:09:09.944
Because the show is trying to present Stannis as a hero, I feel like he's the one you would want to back.

00:09:09.944 --> 00:09:13.924
The good guys don't always win on Game of Thrones, so it remains to be seen. You can let me know, you know -

00:09:13.924 --> 00:09:16.876
Which group do you think is gonna walk away from that big fight?

00:09:16.876 --> 00:09:21.804
Do you think that Roose Bolton is gonna be left standing? Or do you think that Stannis is gonna steam roll him?

00:09:21.804 --> 00:09:25.760
King's Landing has it's own internal problems. It's not going anywhere anytime soon.

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:28.608
Nobody is marching on King's Landing before the end of the season.

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:32.100
Just a quick reminder on the giveaway: I'm going to announce the winner of that during the Q&amp;A tomorrow,

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:33.820
so just look out for that.

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:38.640
In the mean time, you can click here to learn all about the Sand Snakes and you can click here for last week's episode.

00:09:38.646 --> 00:09:41.659
Thank you so much for watching. Everybody, let's high five! I'll see you guys tomorrow.

